Here's how to save and restore draft text using Window lifecycle events:

**App.xaml.cs** — Override `CreateWindow` and hook `Stopped`/`Resumed`:

```csharp
public partial class App : Application
{
    protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
    {
        var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);

        window.Stopped += (s, e) =>
        {
            if (Shell.Current?.CurrentPage is NotePage page)
                Preferences.Set("draft_text", page.ViewModel.DraftText);
        };

        window.Resumed += (s, e) =>
        {
            if (Shell.Current?.CurrentPage is NotePage page)
                page.ViewModel.DraftText = Preferences.Get("draft_text", string.Empty);
        };

        window.Destroying += (s, e) =>
        {
            // Android back-button can skip Stopped entirely
            if (Shell.Current?.CurrentPage is NotePage page)
                Preferences.Set("draft_text", page.ViewModel.DraftText);
        };

        return window;
    }
}
```

**Or, cleaner with a custom Window subclass:**

```csharp
public class AppWindow : Window
{
    private readonly NoteViewModel _vm;

    public AppWindow(Page page, NoteViewModel vm) : base(page) => _vm = vm;

    protected override void OnStopped()
    {
        base.OnStopped();
        Preferences.Set("draft_text", _vm.DraftText);
    }

    protected override void OnResumed()
    {
        base.OnResumed();
        _vm.DraftText = Preferences.Get("draft_text", string.Empty);
    }

    protected override void OnDestroying()
    {
        base.OnDestroying();
        Preferences.Set("draft_text", _vm.DraftText);
    }
}
```

**Key points:**

| Concern | Guidance |
|---------|----------|
| Save location | `Preferences` — fast, synchronous, ideal for small strings |
| Save trigger | `OnStopped` (backgrounded) + `OnDestroying` (Android back button) |
| Restore trigger | `OnResumed` (returns from background) |
| First launch | `Resumed` doesn't fire — load saved draft in your page's `OnAppearing` or constructor |
| Performance | Keep handlers under 1–2 seconds to avoid ANR/watchdog kills |

**Don't forget** to clear the saved draft when the user explicitly saves or discards the note:

```csharp
Preferences.Remove("draft_text");
```
